WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.354
A careful ablation isolates the effect of each change.

00:00:03.434 --> 00:00:05.708
Starting from the JAX implementation,

00:00:05.788 --> 00:00:09.397
the phase collapse activation cuts error by eight percent,

00:00:09.477 --> 00:00:13.721
spectral batch normalization trims a further one
and a half percent,

00:00:13.801 --> 00:00:17.792
and the efficient residual block another two and a
half percent,

00:00:17.872 --> 00:00:19.445
all while improving speed.

00:00:19.525 --> 00:00:24.788
A separate comparison confirms that the phase
collapse activation, spectral pooling,

00:00:24.868 --> 00:00:30.957
and the new spherical molecule representation each
beat the prior alternatives from earlier work,

00:00:31.037 --> 00:00:37.190
together driving the QM9 enthalpy error down to
about fifteen point two five milli electron volts.
